workedExamples.solution_text:
a. Divide the collection into $5$ equal groups. Each group contains $20\div5=4$ objects. Mark $3$ groups.
$3\times4=12$ objects are marked.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"geometry","base":[],"semantic":[{"name":"fractionBlue","hex":"D4E8FF","reason":"Shaded numerator area or marked numerator objects"}],"reference":"Source-adapted discrete fraction representation via five equal groups of four; rows make the denominator grouping visible; light fill identifies numerator groups"}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.65cm,y=0.6cm]
\definecolor{fractionBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\foreach \r in {0,1,2} {\foreach \c in {0,...,3} {\draw[black,fill=fractionBlue] (\c,\r) circle (0.15);}}
\foreach \r in {3,4} {\foreach \c in {0,...,3} {\draw[black,fill=white] (\c,\r) circle (0.15);}}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
b. $12$ of the $20$ objects are marked.
$\frac{12}{20}=\frac{3}{5}$

